{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you shall consume all the peoples.</b> You shall consume them and eat them like bread, in the manner of (Numbers 14:9): ״כי לחמנו הם״ — for they are our bread." "<b>Which YHWH your Elohim gives you.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: when they are delivered into your hand. From here we learn that robbery of a non-Jew is forbidden in the present era. And the Sages of blessed memory said that it is more severe than robbery of a Jew, because of the profanation of the Name, and I have already explained this in connection with the verse (Leviticus 25:50): ״וחשב עם קונהו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:29.385224173Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}